# ACCEPTED RISK: nltk 3.9.2 (transitive dependency of textblob 0.19.0)
#
# CVE-2025-14009  - zip-slip in the nltk corpus downloader
# CVE-2026-78683  - unsafe pickle loading
# CVE-2026-79657  - pickle loaders allow code execution when loading a malicious model/tokenizer file
# CVE-2026-79675  - argument injection in nltk's Java tool wrappers
#
# Why not fixed: every patched nltk release (3.9.3+ and 3.10.x) requires Python >= 3.10.
# This image uses Python 3.9, so pip cannot install a fixed version.
#
# Why the risk is low (verified in code): the app never imports nltk directly. The only use is
# home/views.py: TextBlob(feedback_text).sentiment.polarity, which scores a plain string.
# It never calls nltk.download(), never loads pickled nltk models or tokenizers, and never
# uses the Java wrappers, so none of the vulnerable code paths are reachable.
#
# Mitigation and follow-up: no user-supplied files are deserialised. Planned fix is to upgrade
# the base image to Python 3.12 and then bump nltk.
CVE-2025-14009
CVE-2026-78683
CVE-2026-79657
CVE-2026-79675